from pathlib import Path
site=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'site'
def page(title,body,lab='docs',scripts=''):
 return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title} · FokoLab</title><link rel="icon" href="assets/brand/foko-lab-micro.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/v72-tokens.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/v72-lab-shell.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/v76-system.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/identity.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/upgrade.css"><script src="src/platform/storage.js"></script><script src="src/upgrade/registry.js"></script></head><body class="u-page" data-lab="{lab}"><header class="topbar"></header><main class="u-reading" id="main-content"><div class="u-eyebrow">FokoLab · 79.2 integrated update</div><h1>{title}</h1>{body}</main><footer class="u-foot"><span>FokoLab · Dr. Chilperic Armel Foko Kuate</span><a href="release.html">79.2.0 · release and scope</a></footer><script src="src/v76/app-shell.js"></script><script src="src/upgrade/publication.js"></script><script src="src/upgrade/common.js"></script>{scripts}</body></html>'''
pages={
'publication.html':('Publication and research boundaries','''<p>The public website includes a derivative of <i>Scientific Mastery V6.17 Design Revision</i>. The scientific chapters, section links, worked practice destinations and appendices keep the same physical page numbers.</p><h2>What is distributed</h2><p>Physical source pages 6–9 contain private author-planning material and are replaced by explicit omission notices. The full author PDF is retained, unchanged, only in the complete package’s <code>private-reference/</code> folder. The public-site ZIP and Pages workflow do not distribute that folder or the original rollback archive.</p><p><a href="book.html">Open the book</a> · <a href="materials/publication-status.json">Machine-readable publication record</a></p><h2>Three distinct model sources</h2><p><b>New teaching reductions:</b> seasonal plant resources, two-trait evolutionary fitness, the leaf thermal experiment, generation-resolved cell examples and the mathematical demonstrations. Equations, illustrative parameter choices and limits are available in each laboratory.</p><p><b>Retained public research reductions:</b> the 18-state FADNS and four-state fatty-acid models, plus original research-inspired agent and connected-workflow examples. Their presence does not make them complete calibrated research implementations.</p><p><b>Protected or unavailable full research:</b> no inaccessible hosted source, private calibration data, protected C3–C4 implementation or unpublished full research code was reconstructed and certified by this release.</p><h2>Code and source attribution</h2><p>Existing source acknowledgements, creator pages and collaborator attribution are retained. References to notebooks in the book describe the book’s source ecosystem; they do not assert that those notebook files are bundled in this website. No missing notebook has been fabricated.</p><p>The exact source/public PDF hashes are recorded in the publication record. A hash verifies file identity, not scientific validity or distribution rights.</p>'''),
'release.html':('79.2.0 · integrated application update','''<p>This distribution extends the supplied 79.1 application. It is not a recovered release of the inaccessible newer hosted site, and it does not claim that the hosted site was changed.</p><h2>Preserved scientific workspaces</h2><p>The original model-authoring, ODE, stochastic, equilibrium, bifurcation, optimization, sensitivity, statistics, fitting, ML, AI, SciML, agent, genetics, symbolic, linear-algebra and network implementations remain available. Original equations, catalogue destinations, structured imports, numerical settings and independent plot selectors are retained.</p><p><a href="labs.html">All laboratories</a> · <a href="examples.html">Complete catalogue</a> · <a href="studio.html?preset=original_fadns">18-state FADNS in Studio</a></p><h2>Integrated additions</h2><p>Nine domain entry points add finite seasonal plant resources, leaf physiology, seasonal trait evolution, direct original lipid models, T-cell generations, random processes, branching, conservative diffusion and fractals. They appear in platform navigation and the catalogue rather than replacing the original methods.</p><p>The additive laboratories separate compute, cancellation, replay, pinned comparisons and outdated results. CSV, JSON, SVG, PNG, figure HTML and native Python reference exports retain the explicit request. New analyses do not inherit old test certificates.</p><h2>Release evidence</h2><p><a href="release-evidence.json">Executed checks and scope</a> · <a href="preservation.json">Source and capability preservation record</a></p><p>The release distinguishes executed checks, failed checks, blocked checks and work not run. Controlled browser fixtures are not real-device tests or proof of deployed-site behavior. Scientific adequacy still depends on the question, observational evidence and stated model domain.</p><h2>Reversible source</h2><p>The complete author ZIP retains the original 79.1 archive in <code>rollback/</code> and an explicit file-change record. Only <code>site/</code> is a deployment target. The public-site ZIP excludes private references and historical author-planning documents.</p>'''),
 'trust.html':('Scientific scope and numerical evidence','''<p>A rendered plot is not a validation certificate. Model assumptions, numerical execution, observation semantics and empirical adequacy are separate claims.</p><h2>Original numerical tools are retained</h2><p>Use the method-specific diagnostics in the <a href="optimization.html">optimization</a>, <a href="sensitivity.html">sensitivity</a>, <a href="fitting.html">fitting</a>, <a href="statistics.html">statistics</a> and other original laboratories. Their original source implementations have not been replaced with smaller demonstrations.</p><h2>New biological experiments</h2><p><b>Plant resources:</b> finite carbon, water and nitrogen ledgers; explicit precipitation, irrigation, tissue turnover, mineralization, leaching, single-season senescence and seed-bank carry-over. Net carbon production is a leaf-carbon-dependent phenomenological response. Root hydraulics, stomatal optimization, leaf area dynamics and calibrated yield prediction are not implemented.</p><p><b>Leaf physiology:</b> a fixed-kinetics C3 Rubisco/light limitation calculation, and a separate dynamic heat-balance experiment with prescribed transpiration. These are not a coupled C3/C4/CAM research physiology model.</p><p><b>Adaptation:</b> a newly authored finite-season fitness proxy and weak-mutation Moran substitutions. The season samples a stated window of the environmental cycle. C3/intermediate/C4 shading is an illustrative trait legend, not an inferred boundary or evidence of an evolutionary pathway.</p><p><b>T cells:</b> a finite-generation ODE teaching model. Original agent and connected-research workflows remain available. Neither is a replacement for full Smith–Martin, Cyton or patient-data inference.</p><h2>Fatty-acid interpretation remains qualified</h2><p>The original 18-state FADNS and four-pool fatty-acid equations are unchanged. Total FAS occupancy and numerical reference comparisons can test those equations’ implementation. They do not validate a calibrated mechanism or establish bistability.</p><p>The relationship between the source research bistability claim and a browser uniqueness argument is not resolved here. The original full equations, parameter assumptions, admissible domain and independent analysis would have to be compared. No equation or tolerance was changed merely to obtain an expected number of steady states.</p><h2>How to read the tests</h2><p>Analytic limits, conserved quantities, independently executed Python calculations and known-answer core probes are stronger than import-only checks. Nevertheless, their scope is bounded. Historical test totals are retained only as historical documents in the author package and do not certify this release.</p><p><a href="release-evidence.json">Current execution record</a> · <a href="preservation.json">Preservation evidence</a> · <a href="publication.html">Publication boundary</a></p>'''),
'practice.html':('Worked calculation companions','''<p>Twelve additional worked companions sit beside the original V6.17 lessons, section navigation and 54 source practice solutions. A companion is not a transcription of the book or a claim to have completed its research investigations.</p><div class="u-exportbar"><a class="u-button" href="book.html">Book and source practices</a><a class="u-button" href="learn.html">Original worked lessons</a><a class="u-button" href="programme.html">Research programme</a></div><label for="companionSelect">Choose a worked calculation</label><select id="companionSelect" style="width:100%;margin:12px 0"></select><article id="companionContent"></article>''')}
for file,(title,body) in pages.items():
 scripts='<script type="module" src="src/upgrade/practice.mjs"></script>' if file=='practice.html' else ''
 (site/file).write_text(page(title,body,'practice' if file=='practice.html' else 'trust' if file=='trust.html' else 'docs',scripts))
